| **Annual Paid Leave** | • Full‑time employees receive **20 days** of paid annual leave per calendar year. <br>• Submit leave requests via the HR portal **at least 5 working days in advance**. <br>• You may carry forward up to **5 unused days** to the next year. |
| **Sick Leave** | • Separate from annual leave: **10 paid sick days** per year. <br>• A medical certificate is required for sick leave lasting **more than 2 consecutive days**. |
| **Probationary Employees** | • During the 3‑month probation period, you are **not eligible for paid leave**. <br>• Unpaid leave may be taken in emergencies, but it requires manager approval. |
| **Compensatory Leave for Working on Holidays** | • If you work on a public holiday, you must take compensatory leave at a mutually agreed time (usually within the same month). |

**How to use this information**

1. **Plan ahead** – If you need time off, submit your request through the HR portal at least 5 days before the start date.  
2. **Track carry‑over** – Keep an eye on your remaining annual leave; you can only carry forward up to 5 days.  
3. **Check the holiday calendar** – The official list of public holidays is posted by HR each year; refer to it to avoid scheduling conflicts.  
4. **Ask your manager** – For any special circumstances (e.g., working on a holiday or needing unpaid leave during probation), discuss with your manager first.

